      "name": "life",
      "cels": [
        {
          "key": "life.A1",
          "celType": "FormulaCel",
          "metadata": {
            "key": "life.A1",
            "segment": "life",
            "name": "A1",
            "description": "the =view() pane: run/stop + the canvas painting the B11 grid one rect per live cell. References B11 so every committed generation repaints.",
            "parser": "infix"
          },
          "f": "=view(\"🦠 automaton\", dom(\"div\", style(\"padding\", \".4rem\", \"display\", \"flex\", \"flex-direction\", \"column\", \"gap\", \".4rem\"),\n\tdom(\"div\", style(\"display\", \"flex\", \"gap\", \".6rem\"),\n\t\tdom(\"button\", on(\"click\", \"sim.run\", \"life.B13\"), \"▶ run\"),\n\t\tdom(\"button\", on(\"click\", \"sim.stop\", \"life.B13\"), \"⏸ stop\")),\n\tcanvas(B6, B7, rect(0, 0, B6, B7, \"#101418\"), gridops(rect, B11, B3, B4, B5, \"#7cfc00\"))))"
        },
        {
          "key": "life.A2",
          "celType": "ValueCel",
          "metadata": {
            "key": "life.A2",
            "segment": "life",
            "name": "A2",
            "description": "rule label"
          },
          "v": "rule =LAMBDA — EDIT ME"
        },
        {
          "key": "life.B2",
          "celType": "FormulaCel",
          "metadata": {
            "key": "life.B2",
            "segment": "life",
            "name": "B2",
            "description": "THE RULE, legible tier: the automaton kernel ABI - (alive, n) -> 0|1, where n = live 8-neighbours. This IS Conway: dead+3 born, live+2/3 survives. EDIT ME mid-run (HighLife: born on 3 OR 6) - B12 swaps between this and the wat twin.",
            "parser": "infix"
          },
          "f": "=LAMBDA(alive, n,\n\tIF(alive > 0,\n\t\tIF(OR(n = 2, n = 3), 1, 0),\n\t\tIF(n = 3, 1, 0)))"
        },
        {
          "key": "life.A3",
          "celType": "ValueCel",
          "metadata": {
            "key": "life.A3",
